// The `locale` namespace (area 10, "Locales"). Each operation is listed in
// `jadpo-std`'s operation table with the Rust function in `jadpo-value`
// that runs it, given the locales the application supports.
//
// `from_accept_language` is a pure function of the header and the
// application's `locales { }`, so it gives the same `Locale` in the
// interpreter and in every compiled target. `header` is passed whether or
// not a request sent one: a header read with `optional: true` is `Text?`
// and goes straight in, and `none` gives `locales { default: }`.

public library locale {
    /// Which way `value`'s text runs, as CLDR says: `TextDirection.left_to_right`
    /// for English, `TextDirection.right_to_left` for Arabic and Hebrew.
    function direction(value: Locale) -> TextDirection {}

    /// The supported `Locale` an `Accept-Language` header asks for, or
    /// `locales { default: }` when it names none the application
    /// supports, is malformed or is `none`.
    function from_accept_language(header: Text?) -> Locale {}
}
